# UST.G3BU H02 Endpoint Determinant CRT Campaign

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_MULTIPRIME_DETERMINANT_SCREEN_PROMOTION_OPEN`

## Theorem

Evaluate the exact selected G3BI H02 endpoint determinant at all six roots of
the selected sextic over each of eight completely split primes:

```text
21817, 33863, 37493, 38113, 68213, 69011, 72271, 73673.
```

All `48` determinant residues are nonzero. For every prime, the six values
interpolate exactly to one degree-less-than-six power-basis residue. The full
CRT modulus has `125` bits.

Every proper prime prefix was then tested against the next independent prime.
The seven-prime candidate predicts `0/6` coefficients at the eighth prime;
all earlier prefix holdouts also predict `0/6`. Therefore the current centered
CRT representatives are not stable and cannot be promoted to the determinant
over `Q(gamma)`.

## Consequence

The finite-field chart evaluations are exact, but eight primes do not close
the characteristic-zero determinant. This rules out reconstructing an
adjugate action from the current residues without either more stable residues
and a coefficient-height bound, or an independent exact determinant relation.

